abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. Over every infinite field, two matrix pencils have strict-equivalence orbits at normal-rank distance at most x exactly when an explicit dilation of the first is a constant full-rank compression of the dilation of the second plus x scalar blocks. With a cited linearization theorem this gives Conjecture 1 of Dodig and Stosic over algebraically closed fields. Lean proofs of the explicit theorem are included. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
